{
  "case_id": "2018-18-15",
  "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul W. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government now appears to agree with our principal contention, deference does not apply in this case. The Court should arrive at that result by overturning the doctrine of Seminole Rock and Auer deference in its entirety."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Even if the best reading of the statute is the SG's in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Do you agree from your study of this issue that the impediments to efficient notice-and-comment rule-making have pushed the government into doing more things in this manner?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But the problem is -- the problem is that the judge, or judges, could come up with an interpretation that says the agency's interpretation of the regulation is wrong, and this is a really important interpretation, it has real effects on many people, and it's wrong, but, nonetheless, rule for the agency under your theory because -- and under the Chief Justice's question -- because there's some ambiguity in it and, therefore, defer to the agency, even though the judges might unanimously think it's wrong. And doesn't that trouble you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the best reading is when you are facing multiple reasonable constructions. And that, again, is the virtue of Seminole Rock."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Should we be concerned about the effect that either overruling Auer and Seminole Rock or taking your position will have on cases in which courts have interpreted regulations based on those principles and now, whichever course we take, those will be thrown into doubt? And if that's a real concern, is it more of a concern -- is it much less of a concern if we take your proposed route than if we overrule Auer and Seminole Rock completely?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL FRANCISCO: I think it's far less of a concern under our rule because -- under -- under the United States' rule, because, under my friend on the other side's position, every single regulation that's currently on the books whose interpretation has been established under Seminole Rock now has to be relitigated anew."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So Auer is gone then. You've -- you are asking us to overrule Auer itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency (VA Board)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Given that suite of factors, we don't think that any individual Board decision by the VA Board reflects the considered judgment of the agency as a whole"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that a bit -- asking a -- a bit of inter-branch disrespect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, if I'm understanding your views, in answer to Justice Gorsuch, you're basically saying a decision by, let's assume, a BIA court is not enough, unless a BIA what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul W. Hughes)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We still believe that the appropriate resolution of this case is to overturn Seminole Rock and Auer in their whole because it's critical to restore the importance of notice-and-comment rule-making that Congress thought was a critical check to bring democratic accountability to the agencies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency (VA Board)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-15",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87dd4503a477016f75e52afe46615d0779fad6d68416f360b78e638eab72954a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87dd4503a477-0003-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "not apply, that is what ultimately leads to stability, because interpretations of regulations would just be like interpretations of statutes that would have binding effect absent the agency or Congress going through the process that's constitutionally and statutorily prescribed for amending the underlying text."
    },
    {
